# Magic Dingus Box — library-deletion tripwire (auditd)
#
# Installed to /etc/audit/rules.d/mdb-tv-sweeper.rules by setup_services.sh.
#
# Why this exists: on 2026-08-02 the TV library directory was deleted four
# times by an unknown actor (31 GB lost) and nothing in any application log
# said who. These watches were installed live during the investigation and
# produced the answer within one strike: Radarr's remove-with-files acting on
# a phantom movie that import_library_movies.sh's unmappedFolders adoption had
# fuzzy-matched onto the "tv" folder. The import script is fixed, but the
# watches ship on every unit as insurance — if any box ever eats its library
# again, `ausearch -k mdb-tv-sweeper` (or grep the raw audit.log — ausearch
# --start has lied to us) names the culprit process immediately, instead of a
# multi-hour forensic session against a cold trail.
#
# Cost: silent unless something writes/deletes under the watched trees;
# during normal imports it logs a handful of records per file move.
# prepare_for_cloning.sh truncates the accumulated log before every clone.
#
# Keys match the live investigation's, so documented ausearch commands work
# unchanged on every unit.
-w /mnt/ssd/library -p wa -k mdb-tv-sweeper
-w /mnt/ssd/downloads -p wa -k mdb-dl-sweeper
